# Deny by default, then admit exactly what the checker build needs. The Worker
# is not built here at all -- it runs on Cloudflare -- but its manifest and
# sources must be present because cargo loads every workspace member before it
# will build any one of them.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!.cargo
!crates
!deploy/pi

# Re-excluded after !crates, which would otherwise drag in ~240MB: the Worker's
# JS toolchain and build output have nothing to do with the checker binary.
crates/worker/node_modules
crates/worker/build
crates/worker/assets
crates/worker/style
crates/worker/end2end
**/target
**/*.rs.bk
